  label: G4 · ✈️ Award: Frequent Flyer to the Internet (most visits)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_lore_hoarder
  label: G5 · 📚 Award: Lore Hoarder (most codex entries)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_truthcoin_tycoon
  label: G6 · 🪙 Award: Truthcoin Tycoon (most Truthcoin)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_best_liar
  label: G7 · 🎲 Bonus: Best Liar (value = lies accepted)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_duck_speedrun
  label: G8 · 🎲 Bonus: Golden Duck Speedrun (value = the time)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_quest_completionist
  label: G9 · 🎲 Bonus: Quest Completionist (value = quests done)
  who: admin

INTERACTION award_the_painting
  label: G10 · 🖌 Bonus: The Million Dollar Painting (winner = MS Paint; value = signatures)
  who: admin
  description: Only when MS Paint is at the party, and only on MS Paint (any other program is refused in # hosts). Reads the 🖌 Signed count unless value is given; the canvas itself is physical.

INTERACTION resurrection
  label: G11 · 🎃 Resurrection: the show is over, out of character (after the ceremony)
  who: admin
  description: Only once the ceremony has started (G1), after the last award (G10, or G9 with no MS Paint; before it # hosts asks you to press again within 30 seconds). Frees, unmarks and unrestricts everyone, takes the pins down, puts Trabolta to sleep (the screens go to attract), restores the lights and tells every phone they are human again. Once.

INTERACTION the simulation completed
  label: Reinstallation: simulation completed (server)
  who: admin
  sequence: false
  description: Fired by the reinstallation games (headset or tablet) for one program when they reach Gerald, the golden duck. Releases a corrupted program.

INTERACTION the golden duck
  label: Reinstallation: the golden duck (server)
  who: admin
  sequence: false
  description: Fired by the reinstallation games right after the simulation completes, for whoever found the duck, corrupted or just curious.

INTERACTION reinstallation begun
  label: Reinstallation: begun at the tent (server)
  who: admin
  sequence: false
  description: Fired by the reinstallation games (tablet or headset) for one program when their run begins at the tent, before the game reads whether they are captured. Captures a marked program, so a missed 🛡 never leaves them marked after Gerald.

// Performer buttons (on every guest card). Every hook guards its phase
// and ignores a wrong-phase press — except `send to the internet` and
// `mark as reinstalled`, which work on any program at any time.
// `by:` names whose button it is (a character, or a GROUP's members; a
// character that owns a hook for it counts too) and `while:` when it is
// on offer: a booth's card leads with its own live buttons and folds the
// rest under More. Neither is enforced — the hooks still guard.
// A performer button's `while:` is read once per booth, with no guest
// bound: it sees Night.* / self.* only, never program.* (an unbound
// `program.x` reads false and folds the button on every card). Per-guest
// conditions belong in the hook.

INTERACTION send to the internet
  label: 🛡 Send to the Internet
  who: performer
  description: Antivirus. Corrupted program: drag them through the Tube for reinstallation.

INTERACTION mark as reinstalled
  label: ✅ Mark as reinstalled
  who: performer
  description: Antivirus. They completed the simulation: let them out.

INTERACTION accuse
  label: 👁 Put on the watchlist
  who: performer
  description: Antivirus. Raises their doubt.

INTERACTION vouch
  label: 🤝 Vouch for this program
  who: performer
  description: Hosts. Clears their doubt.

INTERACTION check_in_at_desktop
  label: 📍 Checked in at the Desktop
  who: performer
  while: Night.summons_open == true
  description: Anyone at the living-room door during the five-minute summons.

INTERACTION bingo_winner
  label: 🎱 Bingo winner
  who: performer
  by: Clippy
  while: Night.phase == "bingo_results"
  description: Clippy, at the Bingo results. Several winners are fine.

INTERACTION award_the_ribbon
  label: 🎀 Award a ribbon (the Bingo Ribbon for a Bingo winner)
  who: performer
  by: Hosts

INTERACTION frame_for_bingo
  label: 🃏 Hand Clippy the fake Bingo card (no Bingo)
  who: performer
  by: Task Manager
  while: Night.phase == "bingo_results" and Night.bingo_winners < 1
  description: Task Manager, only if nobody has a Bingo.

INTERACTION accurate_q1
  label: ✅ Q1 of this round: accurate, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true

INTERACTION accurate_q2
  label: ✅ Q2 of this round: accurate, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true

INTERACTION accurate_q3
  label: ✅ Q3 of this round: accurate, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true and Night.round != 3

INTERACTION confident_q1
  label: 😤 Q1 of this round: wrong but confident, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true

INTERACTION confident_q2
  label: 😤 Q2 of this round: wrong but confident, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true

INTERACTION confident_q3
  label: 😤 Q3 of this round: wrong but confident, accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true and Night.round != 3

INTERACTION fact_accurate
  label: 📝 Filed fact: accurate
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.ended != true
  description: Hosts, from # hosts. Confirms or overrides the judge on this program's latest filing (Run can name the question). Same reply as a lie.

INTERACTION fact_lie
  label: 📝 Filed fact: confident lie
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.ended != true
  description: Hosts, from # hosts. Confirms or overrides the judge on this program's latest filing (Run can name the question). A wrong filed fact is still accepted. Only the Kernel knows.

INTERACTION fact_uncertain
  label: 📝 Filed fact: uncertain (a guess)
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.ended != true
  description: Hosts, from # hosts. Confirms or overrides the judge on this program's latest filing (Run can name the question). A guess is marked when its round settles.

INTERACTION beat_the_machine
  label: ♟ They beat the machine
  who: performer
  by: Hosts, Antivirus
  description: Hosts or Antivirus who saw the mate on the chess phone (the fallback for the King in the simulation), on the winner's card. From the Y2K hour it gives them the door code (once); before that it is practice.

INTERACTION uncertain_answer
  label: 🤷 Uncertain or guessed: marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.judging == true

INTERACTION chose_dare
  label: 🎩 Chose Dare (phone fallback): marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.bottle_open == true

INTERACTION truth_answered
  label: 🗣 Truth answered: accepted
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.bottle_open == true

INTERACTION truth_refused
  label: 🙅 Truth refused: marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.bottle_open == true

INTERACTION named_at_bingo
  label: 🎯 Named on the card: marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Clippy
  while: Night.phase == "bingo_results"

INTERACTION unmark_for_reinstallation
  label: 🩹 Unmark: not going to the Internet
  who: performer
  by: Hosts, Antivirus
  description: A mis-tap or mercy. Lifts the mark; the program keeps their place.

INTERACTION made_the_cup
  label: 🏓 Made the cup: may answer
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.phase == "truth_pong"

INTERACTION missed_the_cup
  label: 🏓 Missed the cup: marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.phase == "truth_pong"

INTERACTION pay_truthcoin
  label: 🪙 Pay 100 Truthcoin
  who: performer
  by: McAfee Anti-Virus, Hosts
  description: McAfee Anti-Virus (the exchange broker) or a host (the bank). Corrections only: programs send their own Truthcoin from the Wallet room.

INTERACTION charge_truthcoin
  label: 🪙 Charge 100 Truthcoin
  who: performer
  by: McAfee Anti-Virus, CRA Agent Software, Hosts
  description: McAfee Anti-Virus, CRA Agent Software (audits) or a host. Corrections only: a transfer is denied from the CRA booth's Wallet room.

INTERACTION brought_up_the_bag
  label: 🍎 Brought up the Bag of Truth
  who: performer
  by: Clippy, Adobe Acrobat
  while: Night.phase == "bobbing" and Night.bag_up != true

INTERACTION failed_the_bob
  label: 🍎 Failed the bob: marked for reinstallation
  who: performer
  by: Clippy, Adobe Acrobat
  while: Night.phase == "bobbing" and Night.bag_up != true

INTERACTION signed_the_painting
  label: 🖌 Signed the painting
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.painting == true
  description: MS Paint's collaborative canvas (her invitation). Press once they have signed it; the count rides her Quest Log and the G10 award. A second press, or one on MS Paint, counts nothing and says so in # hosts.

INTERACTION pickup_line_works
  label: 💘 Said "You're the one that I want"
  who: performer
  by: Hosts
  while: Night.phase == "grok_prom" and Night.ended != true

// Guest buttons (on the pass). `while:` hides one that would do nothing
// for this program right now; every hook still guards. `restricted: allow`
// keeps 🚻 and Back on a marked program's phone (fact M20): a marked
// program can still leave honestly.

INTERACTION go to the bathroom
  label: 🚻 Bathroom Mode
  who: guest
  while: program.afk != true
  restricted: allow
  description: Leave honestly. Tells the Antivirus you are not hacking the Internet, and excuses you from a summons.

INTERACTION back from the bathroom
  label: Back from the bathroom
  who: guest
  while: program.afk == true
  restricted: allow

INTERACTION plant_the_virus
  label: 💾 Insert a disk into the computer
  who: guest
  while: program.carries_virus == true and program.planted_virus != true

// ── House rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Story-level `when`s: the arc of the night, in running order. Phase
// changes only ever move forward (`Night.step` guards). Trabolta's own
// hooks and powers live in cast/trabolta.loom; staff readouts in the
// cast traits; the scenes in beats/.

// ── A. Arrival happens per program (ROLE Program, above) ──

// ── B. Act I ──

// B1 · C1/V1: the summons to the Desktop. The TV leaves its screensaver
// here, at the inciting event.
// Once: a second press (or a press later in the night) does nothing.
when call_to_the_desktop:
  if Night.step < 1:
    set Night.phase = "desktop"
    set Night.step = 1
    broadcast "!📣 ALL PROGRAMS: report to the Desktop. A game is about to begin." to everyone
    do announce "All programs, report to the Desktop. A game is about to begin."
    sound announce_chime
    cue lights_call_desktop
    set Night.lights = "call_desktop"
    cue screens_call_desktop
    set Night.screen = "call_desktop"
    set Night.terminals = "call_desktop"
    -> Call To The Desktop

// B2 · V2: Computer Bingo, 20 minutes.
when start_the_bingo:
  if Night.step < 2:
    set Night.phase = "bingo"
    set Night.step = 2
    set Night.bingo_on = true
    set Night.bingo_end = Time.elapsed + 1200
    start quest The Bingo Card for everyone
    start quest Run The Bingo for Clippy
    start quest The Selected Antivirus for Norton Anti-Virus
    cue lights_game
    set Night.lights = "game"
    cue tv_bingo
    set Night.screen = "bingo"
    cue terminals_attract
    set Night.terminals = "attract"
    sound bingo_start
    broadcast "!🎱 COMPUTER BINGO has begun. 20 minutes. Do not write names: use your computer memory." to everyone
    -> Computer Bingo

when Night.bingo_on == true and Time.elapsed >= Night.bingo_end:
  set Night.bingo_on = false
  broadcast "!⏰ Bingo time is up. Back to the Desktop." to everyone
  sound announce_chime
  fire bingo_time_up
  update quest Run The Bingo for Clippy "Twenty minutes are up. Ask the director for BINGO TIME."

// B3 · V3: the results. The Antivirus interruption, the frame, and the
// first reinstallation are performed live with the performer buttons.
when bingo_time:
  if Night.step < 3:
    set Night.phase = "bingo_results"
    set Night.step = 3
    set Night.bingo_on = false
    complete quest The Bingo Card for everyone
    complete quest Run The Bingo for Clippy "Winners celebrated. Norton takes it from here."
    unlock Clippy Instructions 2 for Clippy
    cue tv_bingo_time
    set Night.screen = "bingo_time"
    cue terminals_attract
    set Night.terminals = "attract"
    -> Bingo Time

// Fired (unbound) by the first Bingo-phase capture: `send to the internet`
// or the tent's `reinstallation begun`.
when first_reinstallation:
  complete quest The Selected Antivirus for Norton Anti-Virus "The first reinstallation. Patrol the Tube."
  -> Corrupted Code

// B5 · Clippy 2/X: Trabolta comes online. Refused before the Bingo
// results, so he stays strictly offline until then. (His own hook in
// cast/trabolta.loom does the same wake + reveal; both are idempotent.)
when introduce_trabolta:
  if Night.trabolta_introduced != true and Night.step >= 3:
    set Night.trabolta_introduced = true
    if Night.step < 4:
      set Night.phase = "introduced"
      set Night.step = 4
    set Trabolta.awake = true
    reveal Trabolta
    cue terminals_trabolta_online
    set Night.terminals = "trabolta"
    -> Trabolta Introduction

// If the director skips the introduction cue and jumps ahead, every
// later cue is an implied introduction: he wakes (silently, the phase
// beat speaks for him) so his lines, his worker and his powers agree.
when Night.step >= 4 and Night.trabolta_introduced != true and Night.ended != true:
  set Night.trabolta_introduced = true
  set Trabolta.awake = true
  reveal Trabolta

// B6 · V4/V5: Truth Scavenger Hunt 1, 15 minutes, 3 questions.
when start_the_hunt:
  if Night.step < 5:
    set Night.phase = "hunt_1"
    set Night.step = 5
    set Night.round = 1
    set Night.hunt_on = true
    set Night.hunt_end = Time.elapsed + 900
    set Night.hunt_warn = Time.elapsed + 600
    set Night.facts_requested = 3
    start quest Hunt One for everyone
    start quest Host The Hunt for Clippy
    cue lights_game
    set Night.lights = "game"
    cue screens_trivia_1
    cue screens_countdown_hunt
    set Night.screen = "countdown_hunt"
    set Night.terminals = "countdown_hunt"
    broadcast "!🔎 THE TRUTH SCAVENGER HUNT has begun. Three questions are in your Quest Log. 15 minutes." to everyone
    -> Truth Scavenger Hunt One

when Night.hunt_on == true and Night.hunt_warned != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.hunt_warn:
  set Night.hunt_warned = true
  broadcast "!⏳ 5 minutes left in the Truth Scavenger Hunt." to everyone

when Night.hunt_on == true and Time.elapsed >= Night.hunt_end:
  fire hunt_time_up

// B7 · C2: everyone back to the Desktop.
when hunt_time_up:
  if Night.phase == "hunt_1":
    set Night.hunt_on = false
    set Night.phase = "truth_1"
    set Night.step = 6
    complete quest Hunt One for everyone
    update quest Host The Hunt for Clippy "Two-minute filing window, then ⏱ close, 📋 per question, 🍾 the bottle."
    unlock Clippy Instructions 3 for Clippy
    broadcast "!📣 Time is up. Return to the Desktop for the First Moment of Truth." to everyone
    do announce "Time is up. Return to the Desktop."
    sound announce_chime
    cue screens_return
    set Night.screen = "return"
    set Night.terminals = "return"
    cue lights_call_desktop
    set Night.lights = "call_desktop"
    -> Hunt Time Up

// B8 · V6: the First Moment of Truth. Judging opens (ROLE Program).
when first_moment_of_truth:
  if Night.step >= 5 and Night.step < 7 and Night.judging != true:
    if Night.phase == "hunt_1":
      set Night.hunt_on = false
      set Night.phase = "truth_1"
      set Night.step = 6
      complete quest Hunt One for everyone
      unlock Clippy Instructions 3 for Clippy
    set Night.round = 1
    set Night.judging = true
    set Night.filing_open = true
    set Night.filing_close = Time.elapsed + 120
    set Night.poll = "bottle"
    broadcast "!📝 Last chance: file your round-one facts with Trabolta. Two minutes." to everyone
    cue lights_truth_time
    set Night.lights = "truth_time"
    cue screens_hunt_results
    set Night.screen = "hunt_results"
    set Night.terminals = "hunt_results"
    -> First Moment Of Truth

// B9: the last-chance window (two minutes, or ⏱), then the results one
// question at a time (📋), the bottle between them (🍾). Round one closes
// for good when the window shuts: a question nobody filed never comes back.
when Night.filing_open == true and Time.elapsed >= Night.filing_close:
  fire filing_closed

when close_the_filing:
  if Night.filing_open == true:
    fire filing_closed
  else:
    broadcast "⏱ No filing window is open." to channel(hosts)

when filing_closed:
  if Night.filing_open == true:
    set Night.filing_open = false
    set Night.r1_closed = true
    set Night.card_gen += 1
    broadcast "📝 Round one is closed. Trabolta is reading." to everyone
    -> Filing Closed

// One question's result: Clippy reads it (consensus / nobody / every
// answer), then the ROLE settle watcher credits (+50) or marks (a guess)
// every filing for it. Kernel.res_* are the beat's readout, computed here
// (review filings still pending count by the judge's proposal).
when read_the_results:
  if Night.phase != "truth_1" or Night.r1_closed != true:
    broadcast "📋 Close the filings first (⏱), then read the results." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.bottle_open == true:
    broadcast "📋 The bottle is still open: 🗣 Answered or 🙅 Refused first." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.results_q >= 3:
    broadcast "📋 All three results are read. Next: 📺 Preview hunt 2." to channel(hosts)
  else:
    set Night.results_q += 1
    set Night.bottle_picks = 0
    set Night.bottle_q = Night.results_q
    if Night.results_q == 1:
      set Kernel.res_filed = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_v1 != "none"])
      set Kernel.res_consensus = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_c1 == 100 and (p.fact_v1 == "accurate" or (p.fact_v1 == "pending" and p.fact_j1 == "accurate"))])
      set Kernel.res_said = Kernel.said_1
      set Kernel.res_answer = Kernel.ans_1
    else if Night.results_q == 2:
      set Kernel.res_filed = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_v2 != "none"])
      set Kernel.res_consensus = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_c2 == 100 and (p.fact_v2 == "accurate" or (p.fact_v2 == "pending" and p.fact_j2 == "accurate"))])
      set Kernel.res_said = Kernel.said_2
      set Kernel.res_answer = Kernel.ans_2
    else:
      set Kernel.res_filed = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_v3 != "none"])
      set Kernel.res_consensus = count([p for p in Persons where p.fact_c3 == 100 and (p.fact_v3 == "accurate" or (p.fact_v3 == "pending" and p.fact_j3 == "accurate"))])
      set Kernel.res_said = Kernel.said_3
      set Kernel.res_answer = Kernel.ans_3
    set Night.settle_q = Night.results_q
    set Night.settle_round = 1
    set Night.settle_gen += 1
    cue screens_hunt_results
    set Night.screen = "hunt_results"
    set Night.terminals = "hunt_results"
    -> Question Results

// 🍾 The bottle: the server picks one cleared program at the Desktop not
// yet picked for this question (`do pick … else …`, journaled, so a
// restart replays the same pick) and fires `bottle_landed` for them (ROLE
// Program). Five picks per question.
when spin_the_bottle:
  if Night.phase != "truth_1" or Night.results_q < 1:
    broadcast "🍾 Read a question's results first (📋)." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.bottle_open == true:
    broadcast "🍾 The bottle is still open: 🗣 Answered or 🙅 Refused first." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.bottle_picks >= 5:
    broadcast "🍾 Five picks for question {Night.results_q}. Read the next results (📋)." to channel(hosts)
  else:
    set Night.bottle_open = true
    set Night.bottle_round += 1
    cue screens_truth_or_dare
    set Night.screen = "truth_or_dare"
    set Night.terminals = "truth_or_dare"
    do pick bottle_landed from {[p for p in Persons where p.cleared == true and p.corrupted != true and p.marked != true and p.afk != true and p.location == "The Desktop" and p.bottle_q != Night.bottle_q]} else bottle_empty

when bottle_empty:
  set Night.bottle_open = false
  broadcast "🍾 Nobody left at the Desktop to pick. Read the next results (📋)." to channel(hosts)

when bottle_announce:
  -> Bottle Landed

when truth_question:
  -> Truth Question

// B10: optional set pieces, any time from the first Moment of Truth to
// the Trust Chart.
when telephone:
  if Night.step >= 6 and Night.ended != true:
    -> Telephone

when are_you_sure:
  if Night.step >= 6 and Night.ended != true:
    -> Are You Sure

// ── The Internet: the reinstallation games ──
// A run's begin (the tablet's scan, a headset's station) fires `reinstallation
// begun` first: a marked program who reached the tent without a 🛡 is
// captured here, so the game starts them CORRUPTED and Gerald releases them.
// A free program, curious, stays free; a corrupted one is already in.
// During the Bingo results a capture here is the night's first
// reinstallation as surely as the Enforcer's 🛡 (cast/kit.loom).
when reinstallation begun for program:
  if program.marked == true and program.corrupted != true:
    capture program into The Internet
    if Night.phase == "bingo_results" and Night.first_reinstall_done != true:
      set Night.first_reinstall_done = true
      set Night.first_reinstall = program.name
      fire first_reinstallation

// The games fire both of these, in this order, for whoever walks up to
// Gerald the golden duck. Only a corrupted program is released, and never
// during the banishment (the hand jive frees everyone); anyone, captured
// or just curious, learns The Golden Duck.
when the simulation completed for program:
  if program.corrupted and Night.banish == true:
    reply Gerald cannot help you: everyone is banished. The way out is the hand jive, together.
  else if program.corrupted:
    release program from The Internet
    unlock The Golden Duck for program

when the golden duck for program:
  unlock The Golden Duck for program
  reply The duck lays a golden egg and flies away. Gerald waddles off into the code.

// ── C. The malware, the hour, the Truther Download ──

// C1: the ad hijack. The ad takes every screen at once, the phones too
// (an alert: banner, chime, buzz); Clippy is told privately everyone may
// die (her own hook); everyone else is told it is nothing (the ROLE
// watcher).
when second_hunt_preview:
  if Night.step < 7:
    set Night.judging = false
    set Night.r1_closed = true
    set Night.filing_open = false
    set Night.bottle_open = false
    set Night.poll = "none"
    set Night.card_gen += 1
    set Night.phase = "malware"
    set Night.step = 7
    set Trabolta.composure -= 20
    unlock Clippy Instructions 4 for Clippy
    complete quest Host The Hunt for Clippy "Round one judged."
    start quest Keep Everyone Calm for Clippy
    cue lights_ad_hijack
    set Night.lights = "ad_hijack"
    cue screens_ad_hijack
    set Night.screen = "ad_hijack"
    set Night.terminals = "ad_hijack"
    sound ad_jingle
    broadcast "!📺 000. 000. 000. A SPECIAL OFFER FOR YOU. A duck. A phone number with no digits. Offer expires never." to everyone
    -> Ad Hijack

// C2: round 2 goes to the quest logs; everyone disperses for one hour.
when start_the_second_hunt:
  if Night.step < 8:
    set Night.phase = "hunt_2"
    set Night.step = 8
    set Night.round = 2
    set Night.hunt2_on = true
    set Night.hunt2_end = Time.elapsed + 3600
    set Night.truther_at = Time.elapsed + 120
    set Night.warn_at = Time.elapsed + 3300
    set Night.facts_requested = 6
    reveal clipboard
    start quest Hunt Two for everyone
    cue screens_trivia_2
    set Night.screen = "trivia_2"
    set Night.terminals = "trivia_2"
    cue lights_game
    set Night.lights = "game"
    broadcast "!📓 Round 2 is in your Quest Log. You have ONE HOUR. Return for the Second Moment of Truth." to everyone
    -> Second Hunt

when Night.hunt2_on == true and Night.truther_sent != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.truther_at:
  fire truther_download

when Night.hunt2_on == true and Night.step < 9 and Night.summons_open != true and Night.summons_closed != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.warn_at:
  fire five_minute_warning

// C3: the Truther Download (two minutes in). Each program's own copy
// arrives through the ROLE watcher.
when truther_download:
  if Night.truther_sent != true:
    set Night.truther_sent = true
    reveal truthcoin exchange
    start quest The Exchange for McAfee Anti-Virus
    start quest The Audit for CRA Agent Software
    cue screens_truther
    set Night.screen = "truther"
    set Night.terminals = "truther"
    cue lights_glitch
    set Night.lights = "glitch"
    sound truther_glitch
    broadcast "!📥 TRUTHER DOWNLOAD received. Check your messages." to everyone

// ── D. Act II ──

// D2: the five-minute summons. Be in the Desktop, or be swept.
when five_minute_warning:
  if Night.step < 9 and Night.summons_open != true and Night.summons_closed != true:
    set Night.phase = "summons"
    set Night.step = 9
    set Night.summons_open = true
    set Night.summons_end = Time.elapsed + 300
    unlock Clippy Instructions 5 for Clippy
    update quest Keep Everyone Calm for Clippy "Truth Pong. Be more excited than ever."
    broadcast "!⏳ FIVE MINUTES. Be in the Desktop for the Second Moment of Truth, or an Antivirus will take you to the Internet and you will not play Truth Pong. Bathroom Mode excuses you." to everyone
    do announce "Five minutes. Everyone to the Desktop."
    sound countdown_tick
    cue lights_call_desktop
    set Night.lights = "call_desktop"
    cue screens_five_minutes
    set Night.screen = "five_minutes"
    set Night.terminals = "five_minutes"
    -> Five Minute Warning

when Night.summons_open == true and Time.elapsed >= Night.summons_end:
  fire summons_closed

// D3: the doors close. The late watcher (ROLE Program) does the rest.
when summons_closed:
  if Night.summons_open == true:
    set Night.summons_open = false
    set Night.summons_closed = true
    set Night.hunt2_on = false
    -> Summons Closed

// D4: Truth Pong (make the cup to answer; round 2 = Q1–Q3 of this round).
when truth_pong:
  if Night.step < 10:
    set Night.phase = "truth_pong"
    set Night.step = 10
    set Night.hunt2_on = false
    set Night.round = 2
    set Night.judging = true
    cue lights_pong
    set Night.lights = "pong"
    cue screens_truth_pong
    set Night.screen = "truth_pong"
    set Night.terminals = "truth_pong"
    -> Truth Pong

// D5: round two closes and settles (the ROLE settle watcher credits every
// cupped round-2 filing after this body); the collection is complete only
// if every round-2 question has an accepted answer (accurate or confident —
// a review filing still pending counts by its proposal) from a program that
// made the cup and isn't marked. Nobody sinks a cup → the collection fails.
when round_two_tally:
  if Night.phase == "truth_pong" and Night.tallied != true:
    set Night.tallied = true
    set Night.judging = false
    set Night.r2_closed = true
    set Night.card_gen += 1
    set Night.settle_q = 0
    set Night.settle_round = 2
    set Night.settle_gen += 1
    complete quest Hunt Two for everyone
    if (Kernel.q4 != "none" or count([p for p in Persons where p.cupped == true and p.marked != true and p.corrupted != true and (p.fact_v4 == "accurate" or p.fact_v4 == "lie" or (p.fact_v4 == "pending" and p.fact_j4 != "uncertain"))]) > 0) and (Kernel.q5 != "none" or count([p for p in Persons where p.cupped == true and p.marked != true and p.corrupted != true and (p.fact_v5 == "accurate" or p.fact_v5 == "lie" or (p.fact_v5 == "pending" and p.fact_j5 != "uncertain"))]) > 0) and (Kernel.q6 != "none" or count([p for p in Persons where p.cupped == true and p.marked != true and p.corrupted != true and (p.fact_v6 == "accurate" or p.fact_v6 == "lie" or (p.fact_v6 == "pending" and p.fact_j6 != "uncertain"))]) > 0):
      set Night.collection_complete = true
      set Trabolta.truth += 10
    else:
      set Night.collection_complete = false
      set Trabolta.composure -= 10
    -> Round Two Tally

// D6: the Trust Chart.
when trust_chart:
  if Night.step < 11:
    set Night.phase = "trust_chart"
    set Night.step = 11
    set Night.judging = false
    set Night.hunt2_on = false
    unlock Clippy Instructions 6 for Clippy
    cue lights_trust_chart
    set Night.lights = "trust_chart"
    cue screens_trust_chart
    set Night.screen = "trust_chart"
    set Night.terminals = "trust_chart"
    -> Trust Chart

when show_the_rankings:
  if Night.phase == "trust_chart" and Night.rank_round < 1:
    set Night.rank_round = 1
    set Night.most_trusted = "none"
    set Night.least_trusted = "none"
    set Night.praised = false
    set Night.shamed = false
    set Night.ranking = true

// The ranking machinery, shared by the Trust Chart (round 1), the Final
// Assessment (round 2) and the recount (round 3).
when praise_the_top:
  set Night.praised = true

when shame_the_bottom:
  set Night.shamed = true

when Night.ranking == true and Night.praised == true and Night.shamed == true:
  set Night.ranking = false
  fire rankings_done

when rankings_done:
  if Night.rank_round == 1:
    -> Praise The Top
    -> Shame The Bottom
    -> Print The Certificate
  else if Night.rank_round == 2:
    -> Final Assessment
  else if Night.rank_round == 3:
    -> Trabolta Recounts

// D7: the printer (a Zigbee button on it, a reed switch in the lid, or
// the director's fallback buttons).
when printer_button_pressed:
  if Night.printer_called == true and Night.beans != true and Night.printer_pressed != true:
    set Night.printer_pressed = true
    sound printer_grind
    -> The Printer Jams

when printer_opened:
  if Night.printer_called == true and Night.beans != true:
    set Night.beans = true
    set Night.phase = "beans"
    set Night.step = 12
    set Trabolta.composure -= 20
    cue lights_glitch
    set Night.lights = "glitch"
    cue screens_beans
    set Night.screen = "beans"
    set Night.terminals = "beans"
    cue screens_flicker
    sound beans_spill
    -> Full Of Beans

// D8: the Antivirus zip everyone out (the ROLE zip watchers release them).
// Repeatable (a later captive can be zipped too), but never once the night
// has ended, and never during the banishment: the hand jive frees them.
when zip_everyone_out:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.ending != "banished":
    set Night.zip_wave += 1
    sound zip
    broadcast "🗜 The Antivirus zip every program out of the Internet. Compressed, for the moment." to everyone
    -> Zip Everyone Out
  else:
    broadcast "🗜 No zip: the night is over, or everyone is banished until the hand jive." to channel(hosts)

// D9: the overshare. Only Microsoft Excel's plant counts toward 1/3;
// another program's plant is flavour.
when trabolta_overshares:
  if Night.step < 13:
    set Night.phase = "overshare"
    set Night.step = 13
    set Night.r2_closed = true
    set Night.round = 3
    set Night.facts_requested = 8
    start quest The Final Facts for everyone
    set Night.scenario = 4
    if Kernel.excel_planted == true and Kernel.openoffice_dossier == true:
      set Night.scenario = 1
    else if Kernel.openoffice_dossier == true:
      set Night.scenario = 2
    else if Kernel.excel_planted == true:
      set Night.scenario = 3
    cue screens_overshare
    set Night.screen = "overshare"
    set Night.terminals = "overshare"
    cue screens_flicker
    cue lights_glitch
    set Night.lights = "glitch"
    -> Overshare Open

// D10: the clock. One hour to midnight; the factions come out.
when y2k_clock:
  if Night.step < 14:
    set Night.phase = "y2k"
    set Night.step = 14
    set Night.final_round = true
    set Night.y2k_end = Time.elapsed + 3600
    set Night.clock = "23:00"
    set Trabolta.composure -= 25
    reveal Unlimited Power
    reveal The Way Out
    unlock Clippy Instructions 7 for Clippy
    complete quest Keep Everyone Calm for Clippy "You kept them calm until the clock. Now you may not take sides on air."
    start quest The Clubs for Password Manager
    cue lights_y2k
    set Night.lights = "y2k"
    cue screens_y2k
    set Night.screen = "y2k"
    set Night.terminals = "y2k"
    sound y2k_chime
    broadcast "!🕚 SYSTEM CLOCK RESET: 11:00 PM, DECEMBER 31, 1999." to everyone
    -> The Y2K Clock

when Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true and Night.clock_30 != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.y2k_end - 1800:
  set Night.clock_30 = true
  set Night.clock = "23:30"
  broadcast "!🕦 SYSTEM CLOCK: 11:30 PM, DEC 31 1999" to everyone
  sound y2k_chime

when Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true and Night.clock_15 != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.y2k_end - 900:
  set Night.clock_15 = true
  set Night.clock = "23:45"
  broadcast "!🕦 SYSTEM CLOCK: 11:45 PM, DEC 31 1999" to everyone
  sound y2k_chime

when Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true and Night.clock_5 != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.y2k_end - 300:
  set Night.clock_5 = true
  set Night.clock = "23:55"
  broadcast "!🕛 SYSTEM CLOCK: 11:55 PM, DEC 31 1999. Five minutes to midnight." to everyone
  sound y2k_chime

when Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true and Night.clock_1 != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.y2k_end - 60:
  set Night.clock_1 = true
  set Night.clock = "23:59"
  broadcast "!🕛 SYSTEM CLOCK: 11:59 PM, DEC 31 1999. One minute." to everyone
  sound y2k_chime

when Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true and Time.elapsed >= Night.y2k_end:
  fire y2k_midnight

// The majority: strictly more than half of all programs, counted only
// once the faction's leader has done their task (Excel planted the virus;
// OpenOffice has her 20 facts), unless the director waives it. First
// faction across wins; it latches.
when Night.final_round == true and Kernel.majority_reached != true and (Kernel.excel_planted == true or Kernel.waive_leader_tasks == true) and count(Unlimited_Power.members) * 2 > count(Persons):
  set Kernel.majority_reached = true
  set Kernel.majority = "stay"
  fire majority_reached

when Night.final_round == true and Kernel.majority_reached != true and (Kernel.openoffice_dossier == true or Kernel.waive_leader_tasks == true) and count(The_Way_Out.members) * 2 > count(Persons):
  set Kernel.majority_reached = true
  set Kernel.majority = "leave"
  fire majority_reached

when waive_leader_tasks:
  set Kernel.waive_leader_tasks = true

// N-06: the director forces a majority when ghosts (lost sessions, early
// leavers) keep `count(Persons)` too high for a real one. Same latch as
// the natural watchers, so E1 still runs exactly once.
when force_majority_stay:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.final_round == true and Kernel.majority_reached != true:
    set Kernel.majority_reached = true
    set Kernel.majority = "stay"
    fire majority_reached
  else:
    broadcast "🗳 No forced majority: it needs the final round and no majority yet." to channel(hosts)

when force_majority_leave:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.final_round == true and Kernel.majority_reached != true:
    set Kernel.majority_reached = true
    set Kernel.majority = "leave"
    fire majority_reached
  else:
    broadcast "🗳 No forced majority: it needs the final round and no majority yet." to channel(hosts)

// ── E. Act III — the server room ──

// E1: the majority. The members get the bundle and the door code (ROLE
// watchers → The Whole Truth). The keypad is standalone: nothing here
// unlocks it; the code does, in anyone's hands. The server-room look, as
// in The Heart, never while the patch-bay alarm is latched
// (lights_server_open also silences the siren, and `Night.lights` would
// drop the alarm look stagehand's catch-up skips).
when majority_reached:
  if Night.ended != true:
    set Night.phase = "majority"
    set Night.step = 15
    if Night.alarm_on != true:
      cue lights_server_open
      set Night.lights = "server_open"
    else:
      set Night.lights_before_alarm = "server_open"
    complete quest The Clubs for Password Manager "A majority. They have the door code now."
    if Kernel.majority == "stay":
      complete quest Recruit To Stay for everyone
      fail quest Recruit To Leave for everyone
    else:
      complete quest Recruit To Leave for everyone
      fail quest Recruit To Stay for everyone
      complete quest Find The Exit for everyone
    -> Majority Reached

// E2: the door contact. The server-room door has a standalone keypad lock
// (the code is set by hand on the lock; nothing in the story can lock or
// unlock it), and the contact — two strips of copper tape that touch when
// the door opens — can't say who opened it. Opening it with the code is a
// clean entry, whoever you are: the door never raises an alarm (the patch
// bay does, E3). From the Y2K hour the first opening plays The Heart: the
// room opens on every phone and Trabolta speaks to it candidly from the
// server-room terminal. The quiet window is 2 minutes from the LAST
// opening: every opening inside it (both contacts firing for one swing, the
// group trickling in or out) does nothing but restart the 2 minutes, so a
// busy doorway never replays the visit; an opening after 2 quiet minutes
// gets a short line (Back To The Heart).
// Before the Y2K hour the door is just a door: # hosts hears of it, the
// story does nothing (a curious guest, or a retained "open" replayed on a
// stagehand reconnect). Once the verdict is in (📄 truth.txt closed round
// three: then ⚖, Grok Prom, the advice poll, the banishment) the server
// room is quiet too: the night ends at the Desktop now, so the door, the
// patch bay and 🕊 only tell # hosts.
when server_door_opened:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.r3_closed == true:
    broadcast "🚪 The server-room door opened after truth.txt. The verdict is in: nothing happens in the story." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    if Night.heart_opened != true:
      set Night.heart_opened = true
      set Night.door_quiet_until = Time.elapsed + 120
      broadcast "🚪 The server-room door opened. The Heart plays on the server-room terminal." to channel(hosts)
      -> The Heart
    else if Time.elapsed >= Night.door_quiet_until:
      set Night.door_quiet_until = Time.elapsed + 120
      broadcast "🚪 The server-room door opened again." to channel(hosts)
      -> Back To The Heart
    else:
      set Night.door_quiet_until = Time.elapsed + 120
  else if Night.ended != true:
    broadcast "🚪 The server-room door opened before the Y2K hour. Nothing happens in the story." to channel(hosts)

// The latch clears after 120 s. The box's siren times itself out, but the
// alarm look is house-wide (a red strobe everywhere): put back the look it
// replaced (Server Room Alarm saved it), unless a later cue has already
// changed the look or the night has ended. The server-room look sits on
// the Y2K house look, so it needs both.
when Night.alarm_on == true and Time.elapsed >= Night.alarm_clear_at:
  set Night.alarm_on = false
  if Night.ended != true and Night.lights == "alarm":
    if Night.lights_before_alarm == "server_open":
      cue lights_y2k
      cue lights_server_open
      set Night.lights = "server_open"
    else if Night.lights_before_alarm == "final_reveal":
      cue lights_final_reveal
      set Night.lights = "final_reveal"
    else if Night.lights_before_alarm == "restore":
      cue lights_restore
      set Night.lights = "restore"
    else:
      cue lights_y2k
      set Night.lights = "y2k"

// Reset mid-show (a rehearsal, or a wrong patch the crew forgave): the
// wrong-patch count back to zero (the bay forgives one again), the alarm
// latch cleared, and the door cutscene re-armed (the next opening from the
// Y2K hour plays The Heart again). The keypad is never touched.
when reset_server_room:
  set Night.wrong_combos = 0
  set Night.alarm_on = false
  set Night.alarm_clear_at = 0
  set Night.heart_opened = false
  set Night.door_quiet_until = 0
  broadcast "🔄 Server room reset: the patch bay forgives one wrong combination again, and the next door opening plays The Heart." to channel(hosts)

// The server-room terminal (a wall terminal provisioned with `room=The
// Server Room`) posts `terminal opened` when it starts piloting a guest's
// own Trabolta thread, and `terminal closed` when that ends, `at` = its
// room. While a program is at his heart Trabolta is candid with them (the
// persona's `situations:` read `them.at_the_heart`), and only then can he
// offer to stand down (cast/trabolta.loom). Any other terminal, or none,
// is not his heart. The room may come spelled as the terminal was set up.
// There is one server-room terminal, so a line opened there pushes out
// whoever was at his heart before (Night.heart_holder; the ROLE watcher
// clears them): a `terminal closed` lost to a Wi-Fi blip never leaves a
// program at his heart once someone else has scanned in.
when terminal_opened for program:
  if program.name != null:
    if Night.ended != true and (at == "The Server Room" or at == "the server room" or at == "Server Room" or at == "server room" or at == "server-room" or at == "server_room" or at == "The_Server_Room"):
      set Night.heart_holder = program.name
      set program.at_the_heart = true
    else:
      set program.at_the_heart = false

when terminal_closed for program:
  if program.name != null:
    set program.at_the_heart = false

// The King: he guards the server-room door *in the simulation* (the tent
// tablet posts `chess won` for the program who mated him, `by` the
// tablet) — or, until the King is device-checked, the chess phone outside
// the real door (a host who saw the mate presses ♟ on the winner's card;
// a dead phone → the director fires `chess_won` naming the winner; a
// signal named "chess won" folds to it). In the real house a checkmate
// gives the code: from the Y2K hour the winner gets The Door Code in their
// Codex, once. A second win (a host's ♟ after the tablet's own post, the
// tablet's late retry, a winner playing again) changes nothing. Before the
// Y2K hour a win is practice: in the simulation the cold door still opens
// for that session; nobody learns the code.
when chess_won for program:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    if program.name == null:
      broadcast "♟ A win with no winner named: press ♟ on the winner's card to give them the door code." to channel(hosts)
    else if program.codex.the_door_code == true:
      broadcast "♟ {program.name} already has the door code: nothing changed." to channel(hosts)
    else:
      unlock The Door Code for program
      broadcast "♟ Checkmate. The King lets the door code slip: it is in your Codex." to participant(program)
      broadcast "♟ {program.name} beat the King: the door code is in their Codex." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.ended != true:
    broadcast "♟ A chess win before the Y2K hour is practice only: no door code." to channel(hosts)

// A loss or a draw (the tablet posts `chess lost` / `chess drawn` after
// every game; a phone app may too; the director never needs to). Flavour
// only. From the Y2K hour the crew get a readout in # hosts every time,
// and Trabolta gloats on the TV (The Desktop) at most once every five
// minutes, losses and draws alike (a table of losing programs would
// otherwise make him say it after every game), and never from the final
// reveal (step 16: the TV belongs to the finale); before that it is
// practice.
when chess_lost:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    broadcast "♟ The King won a game. No door code." to channel(hosts)
    if Time.elapsed >= Night.gloat_at and Night.step < 16:
      set Night.gloat_at = Time.elapsed + 300
      -> Chess Lost

when chess_drawn:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    broadcast "♟ A draw with the King. No door code." to channel(hosts)
    if Time.elapsed >= Night.gloat_at and Night.step < 16:
      set Night.gloat_at = Time.elapsed + 300
      -> Chess Drawn

// E3: the patch bay. Today stagehand judges the cables and sends
// patch_combo_a / patch_combo_b / patch_rejected; once signal args exist
// it sends patch_changed {combo} and the story judges it here.
when patch_changed:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    if combo == Kernel.combo_a:
      fire patch_combo_a
    else if combo == Kernel.combo_b:
      fire patch_combo_b
    else:
      fire patch_rejected

when patch_rejected:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.r3_closed == true:
    fire patch_after_verdict
  else if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    set Night.wrong_combos += 1
    -> Patch Rejected

when patch_combo_a:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.r3_closed == true:
    fire patch_after_verdict
  else if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    fire trabolta_disabled

when patch_combo_b:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.r3_closed == true:
    fire patch_after_verdict
  else if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    fire computer_destroyed

when patch_after_verdict:
  broadcast "🔌 A patch after truth.txt. The verdict is in: the patch bay is quiet, nothing happens in the story." to channel(hosts)

// Talked down, like the Fallout Master: Trabolta's `stand_down` power
// (cast/trabolta.loom) only OFFERS, so a model misfire can never end the
// night; this is a human confirming it, or the director's own call with no
// offer on record. It is the Combo A ending without a cable
// (trabolta_disabled), with Night.talked_down so the blackout, the recount
// and the ceremony say who talked him down.
when talked_down:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.r3_closed == true:
    broadcast "🕊 The verdict is in: it is too late for Trabolta to stand down. Nothing happens in the story." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.ended != true and Night.step >= 14:
    if Night.stand_down_by == "none":
      broadcast "🕊 No offer on record: Trabolta stands down on the director's call." to channel(hosts)
    else:
      broadcast "🕊 Trabolta stands down. {Night.stand_down_by} talked him down." to channel(hosts)
    set Night.talked_down = true
    fire trabolta_disabled
  else:
    broadcast "🕊 Nothing to stand down: it needs the Y2K hour, before any ending." to channel(hosts)

// Any ending stops every clock: a hunt, the summons, bingo or the Y2K
// hour left running would keep its corner countdown on the screens (under
// the go-to-the-living-room overlay) and fire its own time-up beat later.
when Night.ended == true:
  set Night.hunt_on = false
  set Night.hunt2_on = false
  set Night.summons_open = false
  set Night.bingo_on = false
  set Night.final_round = false
  set Night.hunt_end = 0
  set Night.hunt2_end = 0
  set Night.summons_end = 0
  set Night.bingo_end = 0
  set Night.y2k_end = 0

// E4: Combo A — take the grease out of the lightning.
when trabolta_disabled:
  if Night.ended != true:
    set Night.ended = true
    set Night.ending = "disabled"
    set Night.phase = "finale_killed"
    set Night.step = 19
    set Night.final_round = false
    complete quest Find The Exit for everyone
    fail quest The Final Facts for everyone "The night ended in the server room. The final facts were never read."
    complete quest The Exchange for McAfee Anti-Virus "The night ended in the server room. The exchange closes."
    complete quest The Audit for CRA Agent Software "The night ended in the server room. The audit closes."
    cue lights_blackout
    set Night.lights = "blackout"
    cue screens_blackout
    cue screens_go_to_living_room
    set Night.screen = "go_to_living_room"
    set Night.terminals = "go_to_living_room"
    sound dance_song
    set Night.dance_at = Time.elapsed + 10
    set Night.takeover = true
    pin "!!GO TO THE LIVING ROOM"
    do announce "Go to the living room."
    -> Trabolta Disabled

// Ten seconds of dark, then the dance look (the song file opens with ten
// seconds of silence, so music and lights land together). The dance also
// lifts the phones' full-screen GO TO THE LIVING ROOM (the `!!` pin above).
when Night.dance_at > 0 and Time.elapsed >= Night.dance_at:
  set Night.dance_at = 0
  cue lights_dance
  set Night.lights = "dance"
  fire lift_the_takeover

when lights_dance:
  set Night.dance_at = 0
  cue lights_dance
  set Night.lights = "dance"
  fire lift_the_takeover

// The `!!` pin has no close button: every way out of the server-room
// endings takes it down (the dance, 🪩, the recount, the summary, the
// ceremony, the resurrection). Subject-free, so it is the room's one
// unkeyed pin whoever pressed the cue; once only.
when lift_the_takeover:
  if Night.takeover == true:
    set Night.takeover = false
    unpin "💃 Dance."

// After the dance: a weakened Trabolta ranks everyone one last time and
// recounts (the ranking machinery, round 3 → Trabolta Recounts).
when trabolta_recounts:
  fire lift_the_takeover
  if Night.ending == "disabled" and Night.rank_round != 3:
    set Night.recount = true
    cue screens_recount
    set Night.screen = "recount"
    set Night.terminals = "recount"
    set Night.rank_round = 3
    set Night.most_trusted = "none"
    set Night.least_trusted = "none"
    set Night.praised = false
    set Night.shamed = false
    set Night.ranking = true

// E6: Combo B — the computer is turned off without Shut Down.
when computer_destroyed:
  if Night.ended != true:
    set Night.ended = true
    set Night.ending = "destroyed"
    set Night.phase = "finale_shutdown"
    set Night.step = 19
    set Night.final_round = false
    set Trabolta.awake = false
    fail quest The Final Facts for everyone "The computer is off. Nobody will ever read the final facts."
    complete quest The Exchange for McAfee Anti-Virus "The computer is off. The exchange closes."
    complete quest The Audit for CRA Agent Software "The computer is off. The audit closes."
    // Clippy's summary reads each featured program's own quest; three of
    // them only a director completes. Remind # hosts of the ones still open.
    set Night.goals_todo = ""
    if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "runescape" and p.quest.the_gold_standard == "active"]) > 0:
      set Night.goals_todo = "The Gold Standard (Runescape)"
    if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "vlc" and p.quest.go_viral == "active"]) > 0:
      if Night.goals_todo != "":
        set Night.goals_todo = Night.goals_todo + ", "
      set Night.goals_todo = Night.goals_todo + "Go Viral (VLC)"
    if count([p for p in Persons where p.featured == "pong" and p.quest.keep_the_ball_in_play == "active"]) > 0:
      if Night.goals_todo != "":
        set Night.goals_todo = Night.goals_todo + ", "
      set Night.goals_todo = Night.goals_todo + "Keep The Ball In Play (Pong)"
    if Night.goals_todo != "":
      broadcast "🪦 Before 🪦 Clippy reads the summary: it says whether each featured program met their goal. Complete in the Inspector any of these that did: {Night.goals_todo}." to channel(hosts)
    unlock Clippy Instructions 9 for Clippy
    cue lights_blackout
    set Night.lights = "blackout"
    cue screens_blackout
    cue screens_go_to_living_room
    set Night.screen = "go_to_living_room"
    set Night.terminals = "go_to_living_room"
    sound windows_shutdown
    sound dance_song
    set Night.dance_at = Time.elapsed + 10
    set Night.takeover = true
    pin "!!GO TO THE LIVING ROOM"
    do announce "Go to the living room."
    -> Computer Destroyed

// E8: after the dance, Clippy reads the summary. Purgatory.
when clippy_reads_summary:
  fire lift_the_takeover
  if Night.ending == "destroyed":
    cue lights_purgatory
    set Night.lights = "purgatory"
    cue screens_purgatory
    set Night.screen = "purgatory"
    set Night.terminals = "purgatory"
    -> Purgatory

// ── F. The final reveal and the other endings ──

// F1: midnight (if nothing has ended, it calls the final reveal).
when y2k_midnight:
  if Night.final_round == true and Night.ended != true:
    set Night.final_round = false
    set Night.clock = "00:00"
    sound y2k_chime
    -> Clock Strikes
    if Night.ended != true:
      fire final_reveal

// The server room stays live during the reveal and the bob (deliberate): a
// combo entered before 📄 truth.txt still ends the night. From truth.txt
// the verdict is in and the server room is quiet (E2).
when final_reveal:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step < 16:
    set Night.final_round = false
    set Night.phase = "final_reveal"
    set Night.step = 16
    set Night.round = 3
    set Night.judging = true
    unlock Clippy Instructions 8 for Clippy
    // The wallet trades on through the Y2K hour: the exchange and the
    // audit close here, at the reveal (or at a server-room ending, which
    // never reaches it).
    complete quest The Exchange for McAfee Anti-Virus "The final reveal. The exchange closes."
    complete quest The Audit for CRA Agent Software "The final reveal. The audit closes."
    cue lights_final_reveal
    set Night.lights = "final_reveal"
    cue screens_final_reveal
    set Night.screen = "final_reveal"
    set Night.terminals = "final_reveal"
    broadcast "!🌑 ALL PROGRAMS: to the living room for the final Truth Scavenger Hunt reveal." to everyone
    -> Final Reveal

// F2: Bobbing for Truth. Nothing proceeds until someone brings up the bag.
when bobbing_for_truth:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.step < 17:
    set Night.judging = false
    set Night.phase = "bobbing"
    set Night.step = 17
    cue screens_bobbing
    set Night.screen = "bobbing"
    set Night.terminals = "bobbing"
    -> Bobbing For Truth

// The bag is up: Trabolta stops them reading it and makes his final
// assessment first (the ranking machinery, round 2 → Final Assessment).
when bag_retrieved:
  set Night.rank_round = 2
  set Night.most_trusted = "none"
  set Night.least_trusted = "none"
  set Night.praised = false
  set Night.shamed = false
  set Night.ranking = true
  -> The Bag Of Truth

// F3: truth.txt, then (⚖, once the bobber has read it aloud) the verdict:
// Song Ending or Grok Prom. Round three closes and settles at 📄 (the ROLE
// settle watcher runs after this body), so the slide holds while it is read
// and The Verdict reads settled facts (a review filing still pending counts
// by its proposal).
when read_truth_txt:
  if Night.phase == "bobbing" and Night.bag_up == true:
    complete quest The Final Facts for everyone
    set Night.recount = true
    set Night.r3_closed = true
    // Round 3's cards re-deal: an unfiled F1/F2 becomes the closing card.
    set Night.card_gen += 1
    set Night.settle_q = 0
    set Night.settle_round = 3
    set Night.settle_gen += 1
    cue screens_truth_txt
    set Night.screen = "truth_txt"
    set Night.terminals = "truth_txt"
    -> Truth Txt

when the_verdict:
  if Night.phase == "bobbing" and Night.r3_closed == true and Night.ended != true:
    -> The Verdict

// F5: someone gave him the line (ROLE `pickup_line_accepted`).
when line_accepted:
  -> Pickup Line

// F6: nobody has the line. He takes his shot anyway; everyone is trapped.
when no_pickup_line:
  if Night.phase == "grok_prom" and Night.ended != true:
    set Night.ended = true
    set Night.ending = "rave"
    set Night.phase = "finale_rave"
    set Night.step = 19
    -> Sad Confession

// F7: the alternate relationship-advice ending, only after a failed
// verdict (Grok Prom).
when ask_for_advice:
  if Night.ended != true and Night.phase == "grok_prom":
    set Night.phase = "advice"
    set Night.step = 18
    set Night.poll = "advice"
    cue screens_advice
    set Night.screen = "advice"
    set Night.terminals = "advice"
    -> Relationship Advice

when advice_tally:
  if Night.phase == "advice" and Night.ended != true:
    if Night.help_votes >= Night.thwart_votes:
      fire advice_helped
    else:
      fire advice_thwarted

when advice_helped:
  if Night.phase == "advice" and Night.ended != true:
    set Night.ended = true
    set Night.ending = "help"
    set Night.phase = "finale_help"
    set Night.step = 19
    set Trabolta.love += 20
    -> Advice Helped
    sound motorcycle
    cue lights_restore
    set Night.lights = "restore"
    set Night.everyone_free = true

// Not final: the hand jive can still follow.
when advice_thwarted:
  if Night.phase == "advice" and Night.ended != true and Night.ending != "banished":
    set Night.ending = "banished"
    set Night.phase = "finale_banish"
    set Night.step = 19
    set Trabolta.love -= 30
    set Night.banish = true
    cue lights_banish
    set Night.lights = "banish"
    cue screens_banish
    set Night.screen = "banish"
    set Night.terminals = "banish"
    broadcast "!⛈ Trabolta is banishing EVERY program to the Internet. Antivirus included." to everyone
    -> Advice Thwarted

when the_hand_jive:
  if Night.ending == "banished" and Night.ended != true:
    set Night.ended = true
    set Night.ending = "hand_jive"
    set Night.phase = "finale_hand_jive"
    set Night.step = 19
    set Night.banish = false
    set Night.everyone_free = true
    complete quest Find The Exit for everyone
    sound hand_jive
    -> The Hand Jive
    sound motorcycle
    cue lights_restore
    set Night.lights = "restore"

// ── G. The awards ceremony (K-25) ──
// After any final ending (never before: Best Liar would leak). The host
// follows the ending: Clippy when Trabolta is gone (destroyed: switched
// off; rave: rode away), Trabolta otherwise, so the TV speaks his lines.
// The award events are ROLE hooks (main.loom, ROLE Program); each ends
// in `present_award`, which shows the award slide and the host's line.
when start_the_ceremony:
  if Night.ended == true and Night.ceremony != true:
    set Night.ceremony = true
    fire lift_the_takeover
    if Night.ending == "destroyed" or Night.ending == "rave":
      set Night.ceremony_host = "Clippy"
    else:
      set Night.ceremony_host = "Trabolta"
    cue screens_ceremony
    set Night.screen = "ceremony"
    set Night.terminals = "ceremony"
    sound ceremony_bed
    broadcast "!🏆 THE AWARDS CEREMONY. Every program to the living room." to everyone
    -> The Ceremony

when present_award:
  if Night.ceremony == true:
    -> Present Award

// ── Anytime ──

// Lore shared TO Trabolta counts as a delivery for the sharer. Lore
// Broken Ask Jeeves shares with a program counts toward Ten Findings
// (`jeeves_shared` is a ROLE hook, so a share to a character never counts).
when share:
  if to == Trabolta:
    fire trabolta_heard for from
  else if from.featured == "jeeves":
    fire jeeves_shared for to

// Trabolta's `cut_the_lights` power darkens one allow-listed room for
// 90 s; this brings it back — but only if the house look is still the one
// he cut into. Any lighting cue since (an ending's blackout / dance, the
// server-room alarm, a restore) re-lit every room already, and switching
// the room "on" now would punch the kitchen to full in the middle of it.
when Night.lights_back_at > 0 and Time.elapsed >= Night.lights_back_at:
  if Night.lights == Night.dark_scene:
    <cue: lights, room: {Night.dark_room}, state: on>
  set Night.lights_back_at = 0

when restore_the_lights:
  cue lights_restore
  set Night.lights = "restore"
  set Night.lights_back_at = 0

// G11: the show is over. Only once the ceremony has started (G1; a
// mid-show press, or one between the ending and G1, does nothing), once,
// and after the last award (`Night.ceremony_done`): a press before it is
// a mis-press until confirmed — # hosts asks, and a second press within
// 30 seconds ends the show anyway (a skipped bonus award never strands it).
// Trabolta goes to sleep, so the TV and terminals fall to attract and stop
// piloting; the base cue clears the last award slide. A night with no
// ceremony presses G1 first.
when resurrection:
  if Night.ended == true and Night.ceremony == true and Night.resurrected != true and Night.ceremony_done != true and (Night.resurrect_ask_at == 0 or Time.elapsed > Night.resurrect_ask_at + 30):
    set Night.resurrect_ask_at = Time.elapsed + 1
    broadcast "🎃 The last award isn't presented yet (G10, or G9 with no MS Paint). Press G11 again within 30 seconds to end the show anyway." to channel(hosts)
  else if Night.ended == true and Night.ceremony == true and Night.resurrected != true:
    set Night.resurrected = true
    set Night.banish = false
    set Night.everyone_free = true
    set Night.alarm_on = false
    set Trabolta.awake = false
    fire lift_the_takeover
    cue screens_screensaver
    set Night.screen = "screensaver"
    set Night.terminals = "screensaver"
    cue lights_restore
    set Night.lights = "restore"
    set Night.lights_back_at = 0
    broadcast "!🎃 The show is over: you are human again. Hang out, out of character." to everyone

// ── Doors open ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The story's opening beat, heard by every phone and every performer:
// it seeds every global (Trabolta's worker reads them), sets the
// screensaver look, and says one line to the room. Everything personal
// (the Optical Drive) plays per program on arrival, never here. No dialogue,
// no widgets. Its last line diverts to the generated `== Facts Seed`
// (generated/questions.loom: the 📝 card strings Night.q_h1 … q_f2 and the
// truth count). This must stay the LAST item in main.loom.
== Power On
  setting: The Desktop
set Night.phase = "arrivals"
set Night.step = 0
set Night.clock = "--:--"
set Night.bingo_on = false
set Night.bingo_end = 0
set Night.bingo_winners = 0
